cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Moth, please cite this software record and the paper."
type: software
title: "Moth: a 19.7 MB Italian–English code-switching speech recognizer"
abstract: >-
  Moth is a very small open Italian + English code-switching speech-to-text
  model: a pretrained Whisper-tiny encoder, two additional transformer blocks
  and a linear CTC head over a shared IT+EN SentencePiece BPE. Release 0.8.1 is
  an 11.9 MB INT8 ONNX graph in a 19.71 MB package and runs in the browser via
  ONNX Runtime Web.
authors:
  - family-names: Bosi
    given-names: Tancredi
  - family-names: Zanolli
    given-names: Roberto
  - name: "Semantique Team"
version: 0.8.1
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/semantique-team/moth-stt"
repository-code: "https://github.com/semantique-team/moth-stt"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/semantique-team/moth-stt"
    description: "Model weights and browser demo package"
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/semantique-team/moth-cs"
    description: "Recorded Italian–English code-switching dataset (CC-BY-4.0)"
keywords:
  - speech recognition
  - code-switching
  - Italian
  - English
  - Whisper
  - CTC
  - ONNX
  - browser
